<http://data.silknow.org/object/58bab03b-a8d4-3ff5-9816-328030800877>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "During the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries, illustrations of biblical stories served as didactic examples of moral behavior. The life of Joseph might represent love of the family while individual episodes could be interpreted differently. The rejection of Potiphar’s wife (on the back), for instance, may signify chastity, an important female virtue."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/bfd1065f-8fd5-34b5-bcb1-c03349bb5ba9> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/bdb4853c-0020-305f-adc9-20ff83539bf7> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/b9ac3e2a-a46d-3a57-92ec-ee1b38ac52e6> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/9e497943-d3ae-3921-b14a-e5241c36a8e9> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/73b46175-5064-3ea7-b3eb-57113f79b3fc> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e2d86135-8490-30b3-91bc-782c5246a8bc> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/09065216-2168-3d6a-8ac9-6640565ab6cc> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/5bea3b29-626f-3b29-9770-69c818b07aa4> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/176ac239-a2f4-3c56-a2fa-2fb5e63fbabb> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/fd79a138-5dc5-32a6-b083-721e62da4a11> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/10ed22dc-4493-30c0-b83d-14315c402264> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/0bc3a1b2-cecb-3c15-8d2b-9b745c1de25c> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/402d8fb8-9e3d-3a0f-a7d8-75d5ad3d5271> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c8ae93cc-d501-3106-b80a-732cbb655a29> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "During the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries, illustrations of biblical stories served as didactic examples of moral behavior. The life of Joseph might represent love of the family while individual episodes could be interpreted differently. The rejection of Potiphar’s wife (on the back), for instance, may signify chastity, an important female virtue."@en ;
        dc:identifier                  "39.13.3a–k" ;
